# HiveMind runs with ZERO required values — `docker compose up -d --build` just works,
# and the first person to register becomes org_admin (no admin token needed).
# Everything below is OPTIONAL hardening for a shared/exposed deployment.

# Change this before exposing Neo4j's ports (7474/7687) beyond localhost:
# NEO4J_PASSWORD=change-me-neo4j

# Vault key. Auto-generated and persisted to the data volume when unset — only set this
# if you want to control/rotate it yourself:
#   python3 -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
# SECRET_MASTER_KEY=

# Operator break-glass. When UNSET the /admin API is disabled and all administration goes
# through org_admin account tokens + registration/invites. Set it only if you want a
# separate super-admin channel (e.g. managing multiple orgs):
# ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Name of the org created by the very first self-registration:
# HIVE_ORG_NAME=HiveMind

# --- embeddings: local by default (fastembed, offline). See INSTALL.md to change model. ---
